    "open_questions": [
      "His own words on his playing: Off the Record (his transcriptions of ten of the songs, with his analysis), The Funky Beat, Future Sounds and the Meronuck dissertation were not readable here; the style follows other transcribers, not him.",
      "Which kit he played in 1972 to 1974: the 1973 films show white pearl shells, chrome lugs and brass cymbals; the maker is not named in any source read.",
      "Soul Vaccination's Songsterr tab: flagged human, but its revision note speaks of correcting a machine's note detection; checked against Earl drum's score only for the verse.",
      "What Is Hip?'s chorus: the score's diamond is read as the ride bell and its circled x as the crash; a second transcription writes the chorus on the hats.",
      "Squib Cakes, Knock Yourself Out and the other Off the Record songs: no human transcription found online to build them from."
    ]
  },
