    "roles": ["band_member", "session", "educator", "composer"],
    "summary": "Tower of Power's drummer from July 1970 to the mid-1970s and again from 1998 to 2024, and the man who put the Oakland in Oakland funk: sixteenth-note grooves with 'all or most of the notes played separately', the hands on the hats and the snare playing one line between them, the backbeat often moved off 2 and 4 into a figure that 'resets itself after a few bars', the hat opened and shut on the off-beats, and a kick talking with Rocco Prestia's bass. What Is Hip? (which he co-wrote), Soul Vaccination, Oakland Stroke. 'All I did was take what I liked from about six or seven of my favorite drummers.'"
  },
